# A great run on the Embarcadero (the score tiers' measure; re-measured after city phase 15 rebuilt Pier 7 as it
# is: its three blocks stand 9 to 12 m apart across the riding line, so a strong player gets one block a pass
# there, and the level's best line is EMB's row of granite ledges by the banks). Every 10 s (the teleport
# stands in for rolling back) at 7 m/s beside the row: a 50-50 down its second ledge (EMB LEDGE), popped off
# with an impossible onto the third, a kickflip onto the fourth, an impossible off its end into a manual, a
# kickflip out: 17,496 x9, landed by 9.8 s; eleven, 192,456. Pro (20,000) on the second,
# Sick (162,000, 84% of it as 140,000 was of the old run's 166,320) on the tenth. A decent run (two ledges popped one
# onto the next, 2,889, every 20 s) scores 17,334. Only impossibles and kickflips: their directions
# (up, left) end no special's keys (right-down, left-right, up-down), whatever the balance bot pressed before,
# so with the meter full the line stays the same line (a shove-it after the bot's right was a Kickflip Superman).
park sf
cmd 0 traffic clear
cmd 0 run level embarcadero
bot balance
cmd 1 teleport 620.42 686.83 -9.3 141.9
cmd 3 set skater.vel.x 4.320
cmd 3 set skater.vel.y -5.509
